description.narrative:
The aim of the project is to enhance climate resilience and protection of vulnerable populations in Africa and Southeast Asia through robust adaptation measures in selected cities by addressing key barriers - such as insufficient data, inadequate plans, weak partnerships, limited financial strategies and budgeting processes, lack of integration of climate resilience into land use planning as well as limited climate leadership and public support. The project will focus on urban flooding, drought, and extreme heat while promoting nature-based solutions. 
This will be pursued through three workstreams: 
1) building the enabling environment for robust adaptation measures; 
2) supporting high-impact actions; 
3) strengthening leadership, knowledge sharing, and partnerships to drive regional resilience.
